---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { ephemerisElements } from "../../data/ephemeris";
---
<SiteLayout title="Planet position explorer" description="Explore approximate heliocentric planetary positions for dates from 1 to 3000 CE using NASA/JPL long-range Keplerian elements and periodic corrections.">
  <div class="container breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/tools/">Tools</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Planet position explorer</span></div>
  <header class="page-intro container">
    <div class="eyebrow">TOOL 06 · PLANETARY POSITIONS</div>
    <h1>Approximate planetary<br /><span class="heading-muted">positions by date.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Choose a date to see the planets' approximate positions around the Sun. The calculation runs in your browser.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section container ephem-section">
    <div class="horizons-access card">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Higher-precision ephemerides</span><strong>Need a live JPL calculation?</strong><p>Open NASA/JPL Horizons directly for selectable targets, epochs, coordinate centres and output tables. This browser tool remains the documented long-range approximation below.</p></div>
      <a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open JPL Horizons ↗</a>
    </div>
    <div class="ephem-toolbar card">
      <div class="ephemeris-date-control"><span class="eyebrow">Choose an instant</span><label for="ephemeris-date">Date and local time</label><input id="ephemeris-date" type="datetime-local" min="0001-01-01T00:00" max="3000-12-31T23:59" /><button type="button" class="btn ephemeris-now-button" id="ephemeris-now" aria-label="Use current time">↻ Use current time</button></div>
      <div class="ephem-status"><span class="eyebrow">Calculation status</span><strong id="ephemeris-status">Preparing planetary positions…</strong><p id="ephemeris-message" role="status">The browser date picker accepts dates from 1 CE through 3000 CE.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="ephem-layout">
      <figure class="card ephem-map">
        <div class="ephem-map-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">J2000 ecliptic plane</span><h2>Solar System positions</h2></div><span class="tag">Top-down projection</span></div>
        <svg id="ephemeris-svg" viewBox="0 0 520 520" role="img" aria-labelledby="ephemeris-title ephemeris-desc">
          <title id="ephemeris-title">Approximate heliocentric positions of the eight planets</title>
          <desc id="ephemeris-desc">A top-down projection of the planetary orbits in the J2000 ecliptic plane. The Sun is at the centre. Orbit sizes and positions are calculated for the selected date and are approximate.</desc>
          <g id="ephemeris-grid" fill="none" stroke="rgba(151,184,220,.12)" stroke-width="1"><circle cx="260" cy="260" r="54"/><circle cx="260" cy="260" r="108"/><circle cx="260" cy="260" r="161"/><circle cx="260" cy="260" r="215"/><path d="M 25 260 H 495 M 260 25 V 495" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/></g>
          <g id="ephemeris-orbits"></g>
          <circle cx="260" cy="260" r="7.5" fill="#edb966"/><circle cx="260" cy="260" r="15" fill="none" stroke="rgba(237,185,102,.28)"/>
          <text x="260" y="286" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e6c88e" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1">SUN</text>
          <g id="ephemeris-markers"></g>
        </svg>
        <div class="ephem-legend"><span><i class="legend-sun"></i> Sun</span><span><i class="legend-earth"></i> Earth</span><span>Other circles: planet positions</span></div>
        <figcaption>Projected into the mean ecliptic plane. Distances use one common AU scale; planetary bodies are enlarged and not drawn to scale.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <aside class="card ephem-summary">
        <span class="eyebrow">At a glance</span><h2>The planets<br />around the Sun.</h2>
        <p>The geometry is heliocentric: each planet is plotted relative to the Sun. The table also gives each planet's geometric distance and direction relative to the Earth–Moon barycentre (EMB), which JPL supplies as a close proxy for Earth's centre.</p>
        <div class="ephem-callout"><strong>What “today” means here</strong><p>The default instant is your device's current local time. The selected local instant is converted to a Julian date from its UTC timestamp. This educational implementation does not perform a full UTC-to-TDB time-scale conversion.</p></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/approx_pos.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the JPL method and accuracy notes ↗</a>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="card ephem-table-card">
      <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Computed coordinates</div><h2>Planet by planet.</h2></div><p>EMB-relative distances are geometric, not light-time-corrected apparent positions. “Light time” is a one-way vacuum estimate from the Earth–Moon barycentre.</p></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="ephem-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Planet</th><th scope="col">Sun distance</th><th scope="col">EMB distance*</th><th scope="col">EMB-centred ecliptic longitude*</th><th scope="col">Light time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {ephemerisElements.map((planet) => <tr data-planet={planet.slug}><th scope="row"><span class="planet-swatch" style={"--planet:" + planet.color}></span>{planet.name}{planet.slug === "earth" ? "*" : ""}</th><td data-value="sun-distance">—</td><td data-value="earth-distance">—</td><td data-value="direction">—</td><td data-value="light-time">—</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="ephem-note">* JPL supplies the Earth–Moon barycentre (EMB), not Earth's centre, in Table 2a. Distances and directions in these columns are therefore EMB-centred geometric proxies; the Moon's position relative to Earth is not resolved.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ephem-method prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Model notes · Read before using</span>
      <h2>Model accuracy and limitations.</h2>
      <p>This explorer implements NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics Tables 2a and 2b: secular rates for the six Keplerian elements, the required periodic mean-anomaly corrections for Jupiter through Neptune, Kepler's equation, and a rotation into the J2000 mean ecliptic frame. Table 2a is fitted for 3000 BCE–3000 CE; this browser date picker accepts 1–3000 CE. JPL publishes nominal errors for longitude / latitude / heliocentric distance: Mercury 20″ / 15″ / 1,000 km; Venus 40″ / 30″ / 8,000 km; Earth–Moon barycentre 40″ / 15″ / 15,000 km; Mars 100″ / 40″ / 30,000 km; Jupiter 600″ / 100″ / 1,000,000 km; Saturn 1,000″ / 100″ / 4,000,000 km; Uranus 2,000″ / 30″ / 8,000,000 km; Neptune 400″ / 15″ / 4,000,000 km. These are nominal model errors, not guaranteed bounds. As a code-regression check, the shared calculation library is compared with JPL Horizons DE441 geometric vectors for all eight planets / the EMB at 1950-01-01, J2000, and 2026-11-08 TDB. All 24 position samples are held within a 1.5× guard around JPL's nominal figures; this is a small set of snapshots, not a proof of accuracy at every supported date. JPL's formula expects a JDTDB ephemeris date; this browser version converts the selected local civil time to a UTC Julian date but does not apply a full UTC-to-TDB time-scale conversion.</p>
      <p>The model is suitable for learning orbital geometry and seeing broad configurations. It is not an observational almanac, spacecraft navigation tool, or substitute for a numerically integrated ephemeris. It does not include light-time correction, aberration, perturbation integration or topocentric parallax. For high-precision work, use <a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">JPL Horizons ↗</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/approx_pos.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics — Approximate Positions of the Planets ↗</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { ephemerisElements } from "../../data/ephemeris";
    import {
      ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM,
      SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S
    } from "../../lib/scientific-constants.js";
    import {
      elementsAt,
      orbitalPlaneToEcliptic,
      positionAt,
      radians,
      wrapPositive
    } from "../../lib/jpl-approx-ephemeris.js";

    const dateField = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#ephemeris-date");
    const nowButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#ephemeris-now");
    const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#ephemeris-status");
    const message = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#ephemeris-message");
    const orbitLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#ephemeris-orbits");
    const markerLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#ephemeris-markers");
    const AU_KM = ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM;
    const AU_LIGHT_SECONDS = AU_KM / SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S;
    const SVG_NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
    const center = 260;
    const scale = 7.15;

    function number(value: number, digits = 3) { return new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: digits }).format(value); }

    function makeSvgElement(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string>) {
      const node = document.createElementNS(SVG_NS, name);
      Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([key, value]) => node.setAttribute(key, value));
      return node;
    }

    function lightTime(distanceAu: number) {
      const totalSeconds = distanceAu * AU_LIGHT_SECONDS;
      if (totalSeconds < 3600) return number(totalSeconds / 60, 1) + " min";
      const hours = Math.floor(totalSeconds / 3600);
      const minutes = Math.round((totalSeconds - hours * 3600) / 60);
      return hours + " h " + minutes + " min";
    }

    function localDateTimeValue(date: Date) {
      const local = new Date(date.getTime() - date.getTimezoneOffset() * 60000);
      return local.toISOString().slice(0, 16);
    }

    function clearResults() {
      orbitLayer?.replaceChildren();
      markerLayer?.replaceChildren();
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableCellElement>(".ephem-table tbody td").forEach((cell) => { cell.textContent = "—"; });
    }

    function calculate() {
      if (!dateField || !status || !message || !orbitLayer || !markerLayer) return;
      const selectedDate = new Date(dateField.value);
      if (!dateField.value || Number.isNaN(selectedDate.getTime())) {
        clearResults();
        status.textContent = "Choose a valid date and time";
        message.textContent = "Enter a valid date between 1 CE and 3000 CE.";
        return;
      }
      // datetime-local represents the user's local civil date. Using the UTC
      // year here can incorrectly reject midnight on 1 January in some timezones.
      const localYear = Number(dateField.value.slice(0, 4));
      if (!Number.isInteger(localYear) || localYear < 1 || localYear > 3000) {
        clearResults();
        status.textContent = "Date outside model range";
        message.textContent = "The browser date picker supports 1–3000 CE, inside the JPL long-range element fit. Choose a date in that interval.";
        return;
      }

      const julianDate = selectedDate.getTime() / 86400000 + 2440587.5;
      const T = (julianDate - 2451545.0) / 36525;
      const positions = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof positionAt>>();
      ephemerisElements.forEach((item) => positions.set(item.slug, positionAt(item, T)));
      const earth = positions.get("earth");
      if (!earth) return;

      orbitLayer.replaceChildren();
      markerLayer.replaceChildren();
      ephemerisElements.forEach((item) => {
        const el = elementsAt(item, T);
        const omega = radians(el.perihelion - el.node);
        const node = radians(el.node);
        const coords: string[] = [];
        for (let step = 0; step <= 90; step++) {
          const E = step * Math.PI * 2 / 90;
          const p = orbitalPlaneToEcliptic(el.a, el.e, el.inclination, omega, node, E);
          const x = center + p.x * scale;
          const y = center - p.y * scale;
          coords.push((step === 0 ? "M " : "L ") + x.toFixed(2) + " " + y.toFixed(2));
        }
        orbitLayer.append(makeSvgElement("path", {
          d: coords.join(" "),
          fill: "none",
          stroke: item.color,
          "stroke-width": item.slug === "earth" ? "1.7" : "1.15",
          "stroke-opacity": item.slug === "earth" ? ".8" : ".42"
        }));

        const p = positions.get(item.slug);
        if (!p) return;
        const dot = makeSvgElement("circle", {
          cx: String(center + p.x * scale),
          cy: String(center - p.y * scale),
          r: item.slug === "earth" ? "6.5" : "4.8",
          fill: item.color,
          stroke: "#f3f1eb",
          "stroke-width": "1.1"
        });
        const title = makeSvgElement("title", {});
        title.textContent = item.name + " · " + number(p.distance, 3) + " AU from the Sun";
        dot.append(title);
        markerLayer.append(dot);
      });

      const body = document.querySelector<HTMLTableSectionElement>(".ephem-table tbody");
      if (body) {
        ephemerisElements.forEach((item) => {
          const p = positions.get(item.slug);
          const row = body.querySelector<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-planet="' + item.slug + '"]');
          if (!p || !row) return;
          const distanceFromEarth = Math.hypot(p.x - earth.x, p.y - earth.y, p.z - earth.z);
          const geoLongitude = item.slug === "earth" ? null : wrapPositive(Math.atan2(p.y - earth.y, p.x - earth.x) * 180 / Math.PI);
          const values: Record<string, string> = {
            "sun-distance": number(p.distance, 3) + " AU",
            "earth-distance": item.slug === "earth" ? "Reference" : number(distanceFromEarth, 3) + " AU",
            "direction": geoLongitude === null ? "—" : number(geoLongitude, 1) + "°",
            "light-time": item.slug === "earth" ? "—" : lightTime(distanceFromEarth)
          };
          Object.entries(values).forEach(([key, value]) => {
            const cell = row.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-value="' + key + '"]');
            if (cell) cell.textContent = value;
          });
        });
      }

      status.textContent = "Approximate positions calculated";
      message.textContent = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { dateStyle: "medium", timeStyle: "short", timeZone: "UTC" }).format(selectedDate) + " UTC · geometric positions from the JPL long-range approximate-element model.";
    }

    if (dateField) {
      dateField.value = localDateTimeValue(new Date());
      dateField.addEventListener("change", calculate);
      nowButton?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        dateField.value = localDateTimeValue(new Date());
        calculate();
      });
      calculate();
    }
  </script>

  <style>
    .heading-muted{color:#8796ad}
    .ephem-section{padding-top:45px}
    .horizons-access{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;margin-bottom:14px;padding:17px 20px;border-color:rgba(230,200,142,.3)}
    .horizons-access strong{display:block;margin:4px 0;color:var(--text);font:600 1.02rem "Space Grotesk",sans-serif}
    .horizons-access p{max-width:68ch;margin:0;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.6}
    .horizons-access a{flex:0 0 auto;color:var(--gold-bright);font-size:.78rem;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
    .ephem-toolbar{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:26px;padding:22px;margin-bottom:18px}
    .ephem-toolbar label,.ephem-toolbar input{display:block;width:100%}.ephemeris-date-control .ephemeris-now-button{display:flex;width:100%;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-top:11px;min-height:43px;padding:10px 14px;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.01em;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(230,200,142,.12)}
    .ephem-toolbar label{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);margin:10px 0 7px}
    .ephem-toolbar input{min-height:45px;padding:10px 12px;color:var(--text);background:#0a1220;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:5px;color-scheme:dark}
    .ephem-status{border-left:1px solid var(--line);padding-left:25px}
    .ephem-status strong{display:block;margin:8px 0 3px;color:var(--gold-bright);font:600 1.15rem "Space Grotesk",sans-serif}
    .ephem-status p{margin:0;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.6}
    .ephem-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.18fr .82fr;gap:16px;align-items:stretch}
    .ephem-map{padding:22px;margin:0;min-width:0}
    .ephem-map-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:15px}
    .ephem-map-head h2,.ephem-summary h2{font-size:1.65rem;margin:8px 0 16px}
    .ephem-map svg{display:block;width:100%;max-height:600px}
    .ephem-map figcaption{color:var(--quiet);font-size:.68rem;line-height:1.55;margin-top:5px}
    .ephem-legend{display:flex;gap:17px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.7rem;margin-top:5px}
    .ephem-legend span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}
    .ephem-legend i,.planet-swatch{display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--planet);flex:0 0 auto}
    .legend-sun{background:#edb966!important}.legend-earth{background:#62a9d8!important}
    .ephem-summary{padding:25px}
    .ephem-summary>p{font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.75}
    .ephem-callout{margin:25px 0;padding:17px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:rgba(9,18,31,.6)}
    .ephem-callout strong{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--gold)}
    .ephem-callout p{font-size:.76rem;line-height:1.65;margin:7px 0 0}
    .ephem-summary .text-link{font-size:.77rem}
    .ephem-table-card{margin-top:18px;padding:25px}
    .ephem-table-card .section-head{margin-bottom:19px}
    .ephem-table-card .section-head p{font-size:.76rem}
    .table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}
    .ephem-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:660px;font-size:.78rem}
    .ephem-table th,.ephem-table td{padding:13px 11px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
    .ephem-table thead th{font-size:.67rem;color:var(--quiet);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .ephem-table th:first-child,.ephem-table td:first-child{text-align:left}
    .ephem-table tbody th{font-weight:600;color:var(--text)}
    .planet-swatch{margin-right:9px;vertical-align:middle}
    .ephem-note{font-size:.69rem;color:var(--quiet);margin:15px 0 0}
    .ephem-method{max-width:850px;margin:48px auto 0}
    .ephem-method h2{font-size:2rem;margin:12px 0}
    .ephem-method p{font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.85}
    .ephem-method a{color:var(--gold-bright);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
    @media(max-width:850px){.ephem-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.ephem-map svg{max-width:570px;margin:auto}}
    @media(max-width:650px){.horizons-access{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;padding:16px}.ephem-toolbar{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:17px}.ephem-status{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:17px 0 0}.ephem-map,.ephem-summary,.ephem-table-card{padding:17px}.ephem-map-head{flex-direction:column}.ephem-map-head h2,.ephem-summary h2{font-size:1.45rem}.ephem-method h2{font-size:1.7rem}}
  </style>
</SiteLayout>
